<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Firuz Shah Bahmani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1397">1397</a>–<a href="/years/1422">1422</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Taj ud-Din Firuz Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taj ud-Din Firuz Shah was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> from 1397 to 1422. A learned ruler, he encouraged Persian scholars and built the palace city of Firuzabad on the Bhima river. He fought several wars against Vijayanagara, but in 1420 suffered a heavy defeat at Pangal, and in 1422 he gave up the throne to his brother Ahmad Shah shortly before his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/firuz-shah-bahmani.jpg" alt="Firuz Shah Bahmani" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Smloverboy4 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haft_Gumbad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
